Summary: Report the composition position, not the whole CFS_RECT area, to the display driver
Category: input
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
Upstream: candidate (draft in .local/bug-reports/). WineHQ master is
 unchanged (checked 2026-11-25).
Why: ImmSetCompositionWindow tells the display driver where the program
 shows its composition (SetIMECompositionRect), which the Mac driver gives
 macOS input methods for their candidate window
 (firstRectForCharacterRange:). With CFS_RECT it passed rcArea, the whole
 area the composition may use, though the composition starts at
 ptCurrentPos with every style (rcArea only bounds it, as on Windows; Wine's
 builtin IME already places a CFS_RECT composition at ptCurrentPos). An
 edit control sets CFS_RECT with its whole formatting rect, and caret
 moves set the caret rect, so the driver's rect alternated between the
 two and the candidate window opened below the edit area, at the bottom
 of the screen, whenever the edit control's call came last. Now the rect
 is at ptCurrentPos, one line of the composition font tall when the
 program set one (edit controls do), else 1 high as CFS_POINT was.
 winex11's XIM spot uses the same rect, so it moves there too.
Programs: Notepad (and any edit control) with a macOS input method
 (Japanese Romaji): the candidate window opened at the bottom left of the
 screen, far from the text being composed
Seen on: macOS 26.7 (a Screen Slots slot, 11.22-build0, Notepad, Japanese
 Romaji: the candidate window at the bottom left, 1 run)
Uncertain: Programs that set CFS_RECT without a meaningful ptCurrentPos
 would now get their candidates at that point rather than below their
 area; none known. A ptCurrentPos outside rcArea (Windows shows no
 composition window then) is reported as it is.
No test: the rect only reaches the display driver, and no Win32 call reads
 it back
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-22: in Second Chance's host8 test tarball, through
 its host, Notepad, Japanese Romaji: the candidate list opened just below
 the caret (1 run). 2026-11-21: imm32.dll built with it, swapped into
 11.22-build0, plain mode: below the composition at the caret (1 run).

diff --git a/dlls/imm32/imm.c b/dlls/imm32/imm.c
--- a/dlls/imm32/imm.c
+++ b/dlls/imm32/imm.c
@@ -2661,9 +2661,13 @@
 
     if (composition->dwStyle & (CFS_RECT | CFS_POINT | CFS_FORCE_POSITION))
     {
-        if (composition->dwStyle & CFS_RECT) rect = composition->rcArea;
-        else SetRect( &rect, composition->ptCurrentPos.x, composition->ptCurrentPos.y,
-                      composition->ptCurrentPos.x + 1, composition->ptCurrentPos.y + 1 );
+        /* The composition starts at ptCurrentPos with every style; CFS_RECT's
+         * rcArea only bounds it. Report that position, one line of the
+         * composition font tall when it's known, so that a candidate window
+         * opens below the text being composed. */
+        LONG height = (ctx->fdwInit & INIT_LOGFONT) ? abs( ctx->lfFont.W.lfHeight ) : 0;
+        SetRect( &rect, composition->ptCurrentPos.x, composition->ptCurrentPos.y,
+                 composition->ptCurrentPos.x + 1, composition->ptCurrentPos.y + max( height, 1 ) );
         NtUserCallTwoParam( (ULONG_PTR)ctx->hWnd, (ULONG_PTR)&rect, NtUserCallTwoParam_SetIMECompositionRect );
     }
 
